UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 22, Lesson 3: Length problems', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Length problems combine measures using addition, subtraction or comparison while keeping units consistent.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nA path is 3 m long and extended by 150 cm. New length in metres and centimetres?\n\nFEEDBACK\n3 m + 1 m 50 cm = 4 m 50 cm (convert 150 cm first).\n\nWATCH FOR\nAdding 3 + 150 without converting units invents a nonsense length.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nSolve eight length word problems (totals, differences, comparisons). Convert to one unit before calculating. Write a sentence answer with units.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"Length problems combine measures using addition, subtraction or comparison while keeping units consistent.","lesson_number":3,"lesson_role":"Problem solving","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA2-GM-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Solve eight length word problems (totals, differences, comparisons). Convert to one unit before calculating. Write a sentence answer with units. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: new numbers solved with visible working for length problem; key places/values named. Do not award marks for retyping the model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample misconception: Adding 3 + 150 without converting units invents a nonsense length.. Correction uses 3 m + 1 m 50 cm = 4 m 50 cm (convert 150 cm first).. Why: restores accurate length problem.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Adding 3 + 150 without converting units invents a nonsense length. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Solve one fresh problem that uses length problem with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Describe one likely mistake with length problem, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept any mathematically valid solution that uses new numbers, shows working for length problem, and names places/values. Reject copied model numbers. / Accept a named misconception about length problem, corrected working, and a method reason. Reject vague “I was wrong” with no repair..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for length problem. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["A claim that names no evidence from the lesson material","A method that skips the key step taught in this lesson","3 m + 1 m 50 cm = 4 m 50 cm (convert 150 cm first)","Adding 3 + 150 without converting units invents a nonsense length"],"question":"A path is 3 m long and extended by 150 cm. New length in metres and centimetres?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for length problem; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["3 m + 1 m 50 cm = 4 m 50 cm (convert 150 cm first)","